{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["And He removed the wheel of his chariots — when the Egyptians saw that they were thrown into confusion, they were struggling with the wheels of the wagons to turn them back, in order to flee and escape backward, but they could not; rather, they were driving and turning them to go backward, and that with difficulty and great hardship, for the wagons and the chariots were colliding with one another. And why were they doing this? Because the Egyptians said: Let me flee from before Israel, for YHWH is fighting — now against us, against Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:28.624974380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}